AB  - Following recent restrictions on TikTok, the mobile application RedNote, originally developed in China under the name Xiaohongshu, has experienced notable growth in the United States. To address the lack of forensic research on this platform, this study presents a detailed analysis of the latest RedNote version for both Android and iOS. A Google Pixel 5a and an iPhone 7 were populated with representative user data, after which images were acquired and examined using Magnet AXIOM and Cellebrite UFED, with validation performed through ALEAPP and iLEAPP. In parallel, static analysis of the RedNote APK and IPA files was conducted with the Mobile Security Framework (MobSF) to identify risky permissions, cryptographic weaknesses, and insecure configurations. The research examines multiple categories of user data, including account details, interaction records, and content browsing and posting activities. The paper also analyzes the app’s folder structure and data storage locations, emphasizing its forensic significance and the challenges posed by its non-international development model and unified APK and IPA releases across regions.
