AB  - Artificial intelligence (AI) has captured the collective zeitgeist; the last five years have witnessed a period of acceleration in AI technological development in almost every aspect of its deployment. Industry 5.0 provides a conceptual framework that articulates AI dominance in not just industry per se, but all organisations and sectors and foregrounds human and robot interactivity where both work together to achieve desired outcomes. This development is also discernible in the criminal sector, where elements of Industry 5.0 are conspicuous. This article provides a comparative analysis of predicted AI-Crimes, as outlined in the 2020 Dawes Centre for Future Crime at UCL Policy Briefing, with real world examples, and evaluates the adaptations to, and impact of, predicted, present and future AI-enabled crimes suggesting a revised impact/concern assessment. This re-evaluation illustrates how AI capabilities are currently being exploited by organised crime with a particular focus on AI-enabled cyber fraud, and how AI-enabled crime can be positioned within an Industry 5.0 framework.
