AB  - Healthcare 4.0 applies innovative information and communication technologies to revolutionize the healthcare sector. Internet of Things (IoT)- based healthcare systems are systems with sensing, communication, and computing capabilities that provide on-demand, at-home healthcare services. The Internet of Healthcare Things (IoHT) system architecture comprises three modules: data collection, data transmission, and data processing, each of which contains several components. The development of technology and prototypes for a technology-centric healthcare system is receiving increasing attention across industry and academia. This survey covers key enabling technologies, applications, and policy approaches needed for implementation. It assesses different research and industrial projects, noting their successes and shortcomings. The study also highlights the importance of Artificial Intelligence (AI) and Big Data analytics for interpreting clinical data to derive actionable insights and facilitate disease diagnosis and treatment. In addition, it addresses privacy & security issues related to patient data. Recent research advances are summarized, and future directions and open challenges are discussed for each system module, thereby advancing understanding of this emerging field.
