AB  - Secure neuro-symbolic federated intelligence (SNSFI) is a revolutionary paradigm that combines the best of all worlds in terms of neural learning, symbolic inference, federated collaboration, and secure computation that seems to offer effective solutions to the ongoing rising demand for interpretability, privacy, and distributed systems of artificial intelligence (AI) models. SNSFI mixes deep neural networks with symbolic reasoning and thus empowers machines to not only learn from noncentralized data but also reason on it, which provides explainable outputs, and it offers structured decision-making. Federated learning also improves on this architecture by enabling training of the model on multiple clients in a way that the sensitive data is not exposed. SNSFI also adopts by design differential privacy, homomorphic encryption, and secure multi-party computation to ensure privacy and trust. Such applications of SNSFI are promising in key fields, e.g., in healthcare, it will run privacy-respecting, explainable diagnostics; in finance, it will enable regulation-compliant fraud monitoring; in autonomous systems, it will perform rule-based safety validation; in cybersecurity, it will augment real-time threat detection with distributed intelligence. Moreover, the combination of symbolic and decentralized neural learning will allow generalization of AI systems, ethical compliance, and scalability to enable real-time and auditable decisions throughout edge environments. SNSFI will, therefore, become an important step toward safe, human-friendly, and reliable AI.
